    <dataqual>
        <attracc>
            <attraccr>Attribute data associated with the NJEMS site locations comes directly from the NJEMS database. Site IDs associated with coordinates were checked with the site IDs in NJEMS before loading site coordinates into NJEMS.</attraccr>
        </attracc>
        <logic>Coordinates from NJEMS were generated and the state municipality and zip code layers were used as overlays to check that there was consistency between the county, municipality, and ZIP code values for the NJEMS sites. Where discrepancies turned up, these sites were investigated and either fixed or discarded. Most of the location in error came from submittal documents and program databases.</logic>
        <complete>There are site records within the NJEMS database that do not have location coordinates derived from GPS, address-matching, or otherwise. As of June 2009, there were 267,561 physical site records in NJEMS. The NJEMSSITE layer contains 165,551 of these, which leaves 102,010 sites that are not represented. Some of the missing sites may include gas station facilities. Complicating matters is that new program site records are still being added to NJEMS, increasing the universe of sites. Often these need to be fixed due to coordinate entry errors. Plans are to GPS sites when possible, and also research site addresses that were not matched.</complete>
        <posacc>
            <horizpa>
                <horizpar>The horizontal accuracy of the GPS derived site locations is typically 1-5 meters. This was verified using digital orthophotography. The horizontal accuracy of the locations derived from 1995-97 and 2002 orthophoto images is typically within 20 feet. The horizontal accuracy of the address-matched locations is probably within 1,000 feet. The address-match accuracy is very much dependent on the GDT and TIGER2000 roads GIS layers. The spatial accuracy of the road arcs, as well as the address coding ranges associated with each road arc are key factors in accuracy of the points matched to the arcs.</horizpar>
            </horizpa>
        </posacc>
        <posacc>
            <vertacc>
                <vertaccr>There is no vertical locational component in the Gasoline Service Stations GIS layer.</vertaccr>
            </vertacc>
        </posacc>
